cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, its task sets or its result tables, please cite this repository."
title: "code-model-reliability: capability and reliability of code models measured as difficulty crossings"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The code-model-reliability maintainers"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  A benchmark of code-model capability and reliability. Capability is the task difficulty at which a
  model's failure rate crosses one half; reliability is the difficulty at which it crosses one in a
  hundred. Both are read from a Bayesian failure-against-difficulty curve fitted to many attempts per task
  on two task sets, wave 1 and wave 2. The repository holds the task sets with their attribution, the
  generation and judging code with the settings every published attempt was produced under, the fitting
  engine, the published fit with the cells behind it, and the figure and page builders.
